nodecode-venice-web is a rewrite of MnrGreg's MnrGreg/hermes-venice-web:

  https://github.com/MnrGreg/hermes-venice-web
  commit dcc286fc40544f4489831ff246de8030fd0417fa
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Greg May (LICENSE)

The rewritten plugin is the whole repository at that commit: a Hermes web
backend that serves the standard web_search and web_extract tools from
Venice AI's /augment endpoints. Its wire is carried over unchanged: POST
/api/v1/augment/search with a bearer VENICE_API_KEY, a trimmed query, a
limit clamped to 1..20 and a search_provider of brave or google; POST
/api/v1/augment/scrape once per URL with the page wrapped under "data" in
some answers; the result fields title, url and content-or-snippet; the
failure shapes (an HTTP status or an unreadable body reported, not raised);
and the key resolution that reads VENICE_API_KEY from the environment, here
with the plugin.yaml manifest's env requirement turned into the cell's
section. LICENSE is the repository's LICENSE, unchanged.

What was left out, and why: the Hermes provider interface itself
(agent.web_search_provider.WebSearchProvider and its registration), because
Nodecode's websearch cell keeps its engines in a fixed list a cell cannot
add one to, so the two endpoints are two tools of the cell's own,
venice_search and venice_extract, with /venice and (help :venice) beside
them; Python's httpx, replaced by the image's own nlk:http; and the plugin
manifest's version and badge fields, which the cell's section and the cells
list carry instead.
